}

\p{\strong{Seeded faults}, in a second private copy, one fault at a time, the rows through the JVM launcher with a session per declaration, the table on, a threshold of one tick and "false" answers kept. A fault is caught when a strict row gets a verdict the official checker does not give.}

\table{
\tr{\th{fault}\th{caught by (strict rows)}}
\tr{\td{1: a constant is named without its level list}\td{6: \code{oh-lvl-const-inst-bad}, \code{-via-use-bad}, \code{oh-lvl-param-name-bad}, \code{-param-vs-inst-bad}, \code{oh-lvl-closure-inst-bad}, \code{-closure-param-bad}}}
