}

\p{\strong{The suite's size.} The four gates through the executable ran while the suite had 1,272 rows; two rows of family E were added afterwards, and the hostile step of each of the four was run again alone on the 1,274 rows: those are the hostile counts above (with 1,272 rows: agree 1,190 and 1,189, the same tolerated rows). The gates through the jars and the matrix ran on 1,274 rows.}

\p{\strong{The two timeouts.} The mutants \code{\verb~|bugs/proj-of-subst-prop~} and \code{\verb~|bugs/rec-of-subst-prop~} with a changed literal need 18 to 30 s of CPU and passed the judge's limit of 60 s on the busy efficiency cores in every one of the six gates, as in the gates of the first wave ([the integration of the first wave](rep-INT8)). Run alone through the candidate's executable they are rejected, with the switch off and on (79 to 156 s of wall clock under that load); with them the agreement is 15,741, the count of the release.}
}

